    "titleText": {
      "es": "Si ves dos números pero son el mismo y tienes que entrecerrar los ojos para verlos, tienes sinestesia, daltonismo, diplopía y miopía.",
      "en": "If you see two numbers but they're both the same and you have to squint to read them, you have synesthesia, colorblindness, diplopia, and myopia.",
      "noteEn": "The Spanish title attribute is preserved from the Spanish archive and the English title attribute is preserved from official xkcd #1213. The raster's circular field contains hundreds of tiny diagrammatic digits: they are audited together as one composite number exclusion because their combined readable result is 42, not a sequence of Spanish lexical units. OCR recognized only scattered, often incorrect fragments of that field; none of those machine fragments is used as lesson text."
    },
