      "questionEn": "How do you say “the interesting one” or “a small one” without repeating the noun?",
      "answerEn": "Keep the article and adjective, omit the repeated noun, and make both agree with that understood noun.",
      "noteEn": "The article is a word such as el, la, un, or una. The adjective still changes to match the omitted noun: una pequeña can mean “a small feminine one,” while uno pequeño can mean “a small masculine one.” Context supplies the missing noun.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Quiero una taza; dame la pequeña.",
